--- A parsed JSON whole number past a signed 64-bit int, within 2^64, is an
--- int with every digit: `type` says int, `int[…]` reads it exactly, and it
--- shows as written. It had been read through a float — `type` said float
--- and `int[…]` answered 18446744073709551616 — in both modes (Rosetta
--- Code, JSON).

d = json['[9007199254740993, 18446744073709551615, -9223372036854775808]']
log[type[d[1]]]
log[int[d[1]]]
log[int[d[1]] - 1]
log[d[1]]
log[str[d[1]]]
log[int[d[0]], int[d[2]]]
log[float[d[1]]]
